hi I'm Erik Bosse and a quiet place is  one of my favorite horror films in  recent years directed by and starring  John Krasinski the movie follows a  family of survivors in a world where  blind alien creatures hunt humans  through sound forcing his family to  communicate with sign language and walk  around like hobbits on sand covered  paths and avoid eating their popcorn too  loudly guys sitting behind me seriously  if you haven't seen it already you gotta  see this movie in a theater sound design  is just nothing like I've ever seen or  heard but rather than just reviewing  everything I loved about this movie I'm  gonna address some of the questions they  might have had the ending the creatures  backstory the families decisions sequel  rumors and yeah spoiler warning if you  haven't seen the movie yet okay let's  get started with the first question what  are the monsters the monsters in this  movie have no given name everything we  know about them comes from notes and  newspaper clippings and Abbot's basement  and of course the way the creatures  stalk and kill people  we know they are extraterrestrial one  headline says invasion with images of  meteors crashing all over the earth Lee  wrote on his dry erase board that they  hunt in packs and why don't they eat  their prey suggesting these beans are  way beyond mere survival they're trying  to exterminate the other noise-making  species and turn earth into their own  natural soundscape other headlines  describe them as indestructible with one  of Lee's notes on his dry erase board  saying armor question mark suggesting  they could have some kind of  biomechanical exoskeletal protective  layer against human weapons and of  course the creatures are blind with  highly sensitive auditory organs that  detect noise even a single word spoken  out loud or a footstep that crunches too  heavily on the leaves the designers of  this movie use lots of real-life animals  to inspire these creatures the creatures  make clicking noises for echolocation a  detail pulled from bats the designers  also said that they looked at  prehistoric fish black snakes as well as  bog people human corpses that have been  mummified in Pete's turning the skin  black and giving it a sagging leathery  look and giving me a new thing to be  terrified of they also mentioned the  Nautilus a sea mollusk with bad vision  their organs are contained within a  protective shell similar to these  creatures but the filmmakers still one  of the creatures to look vaguely  humanoid so they also pulled inspiration  from the Xenomorphs of alien and you can  definitely see that in the odd angles of  the  Penda jizz and the aggressive rows of  sharp teeth now some are pointing out  the design parallels to the demagogue  and of stranger things which yeah it  does feature these opening flaps of the  head revealing the red flesh underneath  really it was important to the VFX  artists for the creatures and organs to  look gross and medical and raw the way  human guts or brains would look which  brings us to our next question what is  the monsters weakness exactly now this  is a central question posed by the movie  itself written among Lee's notes and as  a movie a quiet place cleverly uses the  creatures own strength as their weakness  for one using sound to hunt gives these  creatures quite a few blind spots loud  natural sounds like a roaring waterfall  cover any nearby quieter sounds  providing a safe haven from them the  creatures can also be drawn away by  other louder noises like egg timers and  fireworks most of all sensitivity to  amplified frequencies weakens them which  is what we see in the final scene the  families daughter Regan is deaf and  throughout the movie Lee attempts to  build from scratch cochlear implants for  Regan which I know you can pronounce it  either cochlear cochlear I'm gonna go  with cochlear cuz it makes me giggle  which never worked because Lee is a  self-taught medical engineer using  scavenge supplies unlike a hearing aid  which amplifies sound for the  hard-of-hearing  a cochlear implant bypasses the normal  hearing process it's inserted inside the  cochlea and uses electrical energy to  stimulate the auditory nerve and the  specific frequency of this mount bunk  Shimane cochlear implant disrupts the  auditory nerve of these creatures it  happens on accident a few times with  Regan until the ending when the family  is cornered in the basement and she  turns it back on and presses it against  Lee's microphone the creature freaks out  close up show its outer shell on its  appendages wrinkling and fidgeting as  his head flaps go berserk until it  collapses and it jumps back up exposing  its vital organs and allows Evelyn Emily  Blunt to blast those organs with a  shotgun killing it and then that sound  Larssen more creatures seen on the  security monitors laden Regan to crank  Lee's microphone all the way up to 11  preparing to destabilize all the  creatures in the nearby area as Evelyn  pumps a shotgun like a badass and this  ending answers a few other questions you  might have had like how could this  family survive when the rest of the  world couldn't a quiet place is really  effective at avoiding those sci-fi  horror movie tropes  like one family saves the planet well  first we know that  abbit family isn't the only survivors of  this every day at sundown remember lead  lights at orchha top is great silo  signaling to a dozen others in the area  but for the Abbott's to devise an actual  weapon against the creatures succeeding  where the US military and all the  militaries around the world failed it  still makes sense because their oldest  child Regan is deaf when the invasion  hit they had already been using various  forms of nonverbal communication that  made them better fit for survival  only less than 1% of the population is  deaf giving the abbot's a very uncommon  advantage and that advantage which of  course was disguised as a weakness was  the thing that led to leads construction  of all these cochlear implants that  would later be used as a weapon against  the creatures nervous systems also we  don't know if the abbot's even survived  two of the six of them died in this  movie and for the remaining four at the  end lots of creatures were headed that  way who knows how much ammo Evelyn had  in that shotgun the movies cut to black  endings suggest the fight but not  necessarily survival and now we come to  perhaps the biggest question at least I  had why did the family choose to get  pregnant and about you but when I saw  emily Blunt's womb after the cut forward  and time i was like seriously you  couldn't wrap it up Big Tuna gonna bring  a screaming baby into this world nah  come out with o2 gas every day and put  him in a box for who knows how many  years now I don't think this pregnancy  was an accident  the Abbott's the risk that pregnancy  brings into their lives speaks to the  fiber of their character sure they're  cautious and practical in all other ways  but that doesn't make them paranoid  Hermits they still sit down for family  dinners they pray they teach their kids  math they go out on foraging expeditions  and yes they continue to grow their  family with another child Evelyn's jokes  with Marcus about dying an old woman  they believe in their futures so rather  than seeing Beau's death as a warning to  turn inward and fear they view it as a  missed opportunity to prove themselves  as survivors and protectors oh we can't  protect right after giving birth to her  new son Evelyn tells Leigh I could have  held him now the line is a misdirect  she's not referring to the baby but to  bow on the day he died she could have  held him on the walk back to their home  now Evelyn just gave birth but she's  playing woulda coulda shoulda with the  last kid clearly she sees this new son  this her second chance to survive on her  turns so this baby while super  impractical in this world is this movies  beating heart and from a narrative  standpoint a pregnancy is one hell of a  ticking time bomb and before I go one  final question what will happen in the  sequel the screenwriters Brian Woodson  scott beck said that they were totally  open to a sequel saying it's a fun world  and there are so many other things he  can do hinting at a ton of scene ideas  that they couldn't fit in the movie and  they indicated any sequel wouldn't  follow the Abbott family necessarily  perhaps opening things up to other  survivors in this alien invaded world  now that sounds similar to like a  Cloverfield extended universe  interesting you should bring that up the  writers said that a quiet place was  briefly considered to be part of  Paramount's Cloverfield series but the  writers preferred it to be its own story  in world and here's hoping any future  quiet place movies go further in this  direction specifically when it comes to  the movies bold sound design  apparently woods and Beck's original  script for this movie only had one line  of dialogue I would love to see a  quieter place live up to its title but a  question for you guys what was your  biggest jump scare in a quiet place for  me it wasn't even one of the creatures  whose freaking Emily Blunt just slap in  a bloody hand against a shower stall  door oh god there's gotta be a better  way to get his attention right comment  down below with your thoughts or tweet  me directly at ei vas and follow new  rockstars on Twitter for updates on our  videos like and share this video and  subscribe the new rock stars for more  analysis and deep dives and movies you  love we've done similar explainers for  stranger things and annihilation and it  and get out now you get out of here but  thanks for watching bye
 

